      "side": 1,
      "message": "This pattern seems like it does a lot of unnecessarily repetitive scanning of the power signal lists. In addition, the pwrseq-signal-enum field in the DT binding seems like it introduces an unnecessary level of indirection.\n\nI assume any given platform has a well-defined set of power signals (which may be a virtual wire or GPIO), so rather than having separate lists and needing to scan them, could there be a single list in known order that indicates whether each signal is a VW or GPIO and provides the configuration?\n\nI imagine something like:\n\n    const struct power_signal_info {\n      const char *name;\n      bool is_virtual_wire;\n      union {\n        struct power_signal_info_gpio gpio_info;\n        struct power_signal_info_vw vw_info;\n      };\n    } power_signals[] \u003d {\n      /* Get each required power signal by node name in well-defined order;\n         SLP_S5, SLP_S3, ... */\n    }\n\nThen the driver can index into that array according to the known order of the signals, and required signals can be marked as such in the DT binding.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "524a8d1e50f3a1374a3cd3403b4406552039b80e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
